      ],
      "extract": "0.1. The colored Jones polynomial. For a knot K in S3 and a positive integer n, let JK(n) ∈Z[t±1] denote the n-colored Jones polynomial of K with zero-framing. The polynomial JK(n) is the quantum link invariant, as deﬁned by Reshetikhin and Turaev [RT], associated to the Lie algebra sl2(C), with the color n standing for the irreducible sl2(C)-module Vn of dimension n. Here we use the functorial normalization, i.e.",
      "extractCut": true
