      "extract": "\\label{cjp} By \\cite{Mo}, the formula for the colored Jones polynomial of the $(r,s)$-cabled knot $K^{(r,s)}$ over a knot $K$ is given by \\begin{equation} \\label{cjp-cable} J_{K^{(r,s)}}(n)= t^{-rs(n^2-1)} \\sum_{j=-\\frac{n-1}{2}}^{\\frac{n-1}{2}} t^{4rj(js+1)} J_K(2sj+1). \\end{equation} \\begin{lemma} \\label{J_C} One has \\begin{eqnarray*} && J_{K^{(r,s)}}(n+2) - t^{-4rs(n+1)} J_{K^{(r,s)}}(n) \\\\ &=& t^{-2rs(n+1)}",
